PROJECT: Protecting Source Water & Reducing Wildfire Risk for Rural Communities: An
Innovative Finance Pilot in Wyoming
SUBRECIPIENT: City of Cheyenne
ORGANIZATION TYPE: State/Municipality
PERIOD OF PERFORMANCE: November 1, 2024 to October 31, 2026
PROJECT DESCRIPTION: This project will pilot the potential use of the Wyoming State
Revolving Loan Fund program to finance forest restoration activities on the Medicine Bow-Routt
National Forests and Thunder Basin National Grassland. State Revolving Loan Funds offer
favorable terms for municipalities to fund water quality treatments and wildfire prevention
activities. This arrangement can allow local communities to implement essential interventions
they otherwise might not be able to afford.
